  "reason": "Evidence: config_014 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat, multiprofile, multimodal) achieved 0.518 accuracy, establishing a moderate baseline. With only one data point, the most important uncertainty is whether the simple avgpool aggregation is a bottleneck or whether a more expressive transformer aggregation can better model inter-profile relationships. Question: config_008 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other settings (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, concat, multiprofile) constant, providing a clean single-variable ablation. Why this is the best next experiment: Aggregation is a fundamental architectural choice that governs how multiple profiles are combined before fusion; if transformer aggregation improves accuracy, it unlocks a high-priority family of configurations (configs 009, 016, 018, 035, 037, 043, 049) for the remaining 7 experiments. If it does not help, we confirm avgpool sufficiency and can redirect effort toward RNA encoder or image encoder comparisons. This single-variable test maximizes information gain per experiment under the tight 10-experiment budget."
